  VERDICT: NO-GO. Obstruction: collisional baryons are never cold on FRW (sigma_IGM > 0 at every z) and lose their record by cooling;
  the post-reionisation IGM (12.2 km/s) is hotter than the local gas discs B must switch ON (10 km/s), so no
  constant threshold exists; the variable that has the right properties (cold sigma_c) is MS-forbidden and ON in unbound sheets.
  Conservation is NOT the obstruction: a state-function switch has an ordinary action (D2). Scoped result, not a closure.

